  "finding": "llama3.1:8b does not materially beat qwen3:4b-instruct. Overall means are 0.462 vs 0.523. llama3.1:8b wins on code_heavy (+0.125) and fan_out (+0.250) but loses on medium difficulty (-0.210), long_horizon (-0.200), search_heavy (-0.200), and structured_output (-0.200). Dynamic range does not improve: both models pin ~93% of probes at ceiling or floor (only 2 variable probes each). The bimodal structure of this eval set is model-agnostic at this parameter scale. qwen3:4b-instruct is preferred for Stage C given the existing main sweep data.",
  "dynamic_range_note": "Dynamic range \u2014 count of probes not pinned at 0.0 or 1.0 \u2014 is the key metric for experimental sensitivity. llama3.1:8b: 2/44 variable. qwen3:4b: 2/44 variable. Both are too low for position-pressure effects to show as score changes on most probes. Stage C must rely on specific probes from the rag_*, sea_*, cha_*, lon_* families that have substantial inline content."
